LAST(1)

NAME
     last - list past logins, newest first

SYNOPSIS
     last [-count] [user or terminal ...]

DESCRIPTION
     Reads the login records and lists each login: who, on which
     terminal, where from, when, and for how long.

     With a name, lists only the logins of that user, or the logins on
     that terminal. -count stops after that many lines.

EXAMPLES
     last -10
     last marge

SEE ALSO
     who(1), finger(1)
